From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:02:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop linking the extension manager into WASM

WHY IS THE EXTENSION MANAGER STILL LINKED, DESPITE --disable-extensions?

Because --disable-extensions never removed anything. It sets exactly two things
(configure.ac:3452-3458): the C++ macro HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS, and
enable_extension_integration/update=no. There is no DISABLE_EXTENSIONS make
variable anywhere in the tree -- `grep -rn DISABLE_EXTENSIONS --include=*.mk .`
returns nothing -- and desktop/Module_desktop.mk:15-17 adds Library_deployment,
Library_deploymentgui and Library_deploymentmisc unconditionally. So the flag
only stubs a handful of #if blocks INSIDE libraries that are still compiled,
still registered, and still linked in full. dp_gui::UpdateInstallDialog::Thread::
downloadExtensions() is present in the shipped binary today.

What actually pulls them in is solenv/gbuild/static.mk:66-67:

    $(foreach lib,$(gb_Library_KNOWNLIBS),$(if $(call gb_Library__get_component,$(lib)), \
        $(eval $(call gb_Library_use_libraries,components,$(lib)))))

Every library that declares a .component file is force-linked into the static
`components` library, which desktop/Executable_soffice_bin.mk links with
-Wl,--whole-archive; and solenv/bin/native-code.py emits a static map naming
each constructor by symbol (component_maps.cxx:152-161), so --gc-sections can
never drop them. The decision is "does this library have a .component file",
not "is this feature enabled". Confirmed empirically: all ten
com_sun_star_comp_deployment_* constructors resolve to libdeployment.a, and
libdeployment.a / libdeploymentgui.a appear on the soffice_bin link line
(workdir/Dep/LinkTarget/Executable/soffice.js.d.libraries) while nothing in the
tree references them via gb_Library_use_libraries.

THE CUT

Drop the .component registration for `deployment` and `deploymentgui` on
EMSCRIPTEN. That removes them from gb_ComponentTarget__ALLCOMPONENTS, so the ten
constructors leave services_constructors.list and component_maps.cxx
automatically (native-code.py needs no edit -- static/CustomTarget_components.mk:23
drives it with `-c` from the generated list), and it makes
gb_Library__get_component empty so static.mk:66-67 stops adding them to
`components`.

Library_deploymentmisc is NOT touched. It is a real link dependency of
sofficeapp (desktop/Library_sofficeapp.mk:66) and not because of extensions:
DpResId (desktop/source/deployment/misc/dp_misc.cxx:560, declared in
desktop/inc/dp_shared.hxx:25) is what produces every bootstrap error string in
desktop/source/app/app.cxx (~20 unguarded call sites at :374, :710-750,
:877-935, :1091, :2196), appinit.cxx:356 and lockfile2.cxx:41. Making it
droppable would mean moving DpResId and the dkt .mo plumbing into sofficeapp for
464 KB of archive -- not worth the surgery. Note also that deploymentmisc
declares no UNO service at all (no gb_Library_set_componentfile in
Library_deploymentmisc.mk), so it is not part of this mechanism.

WHY IT IS SAFE

Import/export never consults the deployment registry:

  - filter/source/config/cache/ reads only configmgr TypeDetection nodes; it has
    zero references to deployment/ExtensionManager/PackageInformationProvider.
    (The many "Extension" hits there are FILE-extension matching.)
  - configmgr does parse bundledext/sharedext/userext layers
    (configmgr/source/components.cxx:540-560, named in instdir/program/
    fundamentalrc:6), but that is plain file I/O of configmgr.ini files that a
    deployment run would have written. With a read-only install and no
    extensions those files do not exist and the layers are silently empty.
    configmgr has no link or UNO dependency on deployment.
  - desktop/source/app/app.cxx:185, :462, :1528 are all inside
    #if HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS -- dead here.
  - desktop/source/lib/init.cxx:8506 is inside #if HAVE_FEATURE_ANDROID_LOK.
  - basic/source/uno/namecont.cxx:1175 is dead twice over
    (HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS and HAVE_FEATURE_SCRIPTING are both 0).
  - linguistic/source/lngsvcmgr.cxx:424 and
    svx/source/smarttags/SmartTagMgr.cxx:446 both already catch the
    DeploymentException ("no extension manager - should fire on mobile only").
  - xmlhelp and extensions/source/update are not built (HAVE_FEATURE_XMLHELP=0,
    ENABLE_EXTENSION_UPDATE=0).

There is no undefined-symbol risk: every consumer reaches these through
ExtensionManager::get(xContext), a generated header that calls
createInstanceWithContext by service name. Dropping the registration turns those
into a thrown css::uno::DeploymentException, not a link error and not a crash.

THE TWO LATENT THROW SITES, AND WHY ONLY ONE IS PATCHED

1. comphelper/source/misc/backupfilehelper.cxx:388 acquires the extension
   manager OUTSIDE the try{} that catches DeploymentException on the very next
   line. It is reached from Desktop::doShutdown() (app.cxx:1754) via
   tryPushExtensionInfo(), which is gated on SecureUserConfig /
   SecureUserConfigExtensions -- both `true` in instdir/program/sofficerc:15-19.
   This is INERT on the WASM path today, because doShutdown() returns
   EXIT_SUCCESS immediately when pExecGlobals is null (app.cxx:1692) and
   pExecGlobals is only set by Desktop::Main(), which LOK never runs (see the
   "shortcutting the invocation in Desktop::Main" comment at
   desktop/source/lib/init.cxx:8596). It is patched anyway: it is a real bug --
   the handler for "no extension manager" is right there and cannot be reached
   -- and the fix is three lines of defence-in-depth.

2. desktop/source/lib/init.cxx:7962 SynchronizeExtensionRepositories(true) in
   preloadData() is NOT guarded by HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS, and
   check_ext_deps.cxx:403-423 does not catch DeploymentException. It is NOT
   patched because it is unreachable: preloadData() is called only from the
   `eStage == PRE_INIT` branch (init.cxx:8548), and this project's bridge calls
   lok_cpp_init -> libreofficekit_hook_2, which constructs gImpl before calling
   lo_initialize, so eStage is never PRE_INIT. If this project ever adopts
   lok_preinit, guard those two lines first.

MEASURED SAVING

Retained code attributed to libdeployment.a + libdeploymentgui.a +
libdeploymentmisclo.a in the linked pre-wasm-opt soffice.wasm, by intersecting
the binary's name section against each archive's WASM_SYMBOL_TABLE and counting
only symbols defined in no other archive:

    816 functions, 406,327 bytes exclusive (396.8 KiB)
    + 1,383 functions / 192,077 B shared with other archives (excluded)
    largest: dp_registry::backend::bundle::...::checkPrerequisites  9,736 B
             dp_registry::backend::component::...::processPackage_  9,653 B
             dp_misc::Dependencies::check                           7,463 B
             dp_gui::ExtensionCmdQueue::Thread::execute             7,434 B
             dp_manager::ExtensionManager::addExtension             7,112 B
    plus up to 101 KiB of archive data segments (ESTIMATE of what is retained).

Split per archive (deploymentmisc stays, so it is not part of the saving):

    libdeployment.a        506 funcs  261,349 B  255.2 KiB
    libdeploymentgui.a     242 funcs  116,208 B  113.5 KiB
    libdeploymentmisclo.a   68 funcs   28,770 B   28.1 KiB  (KEPT)

Realised saving = deployment + deploymentgui = 377,557 B (368.7 KiB) raw,
~74.5 KiB brotli, using the module's own raw->wire factor of 0.202
(117,190,355 B linked -> 95,893,393 B after wasm-opt -> 23,700,411 B brotli).
The original brief estimated 106 KiB.

OPTIONAL FOLLOW-UP (not in this patch)

ucb/Library_ucpext.mk registers com.sun.star.ucb.ExtensionContentProvider, which
calls PackageInformationProvider::get() (ucb/source/ucp/ext/ucpext_content.cxx:429).
It only fires for vnd.sun.star.extension:// URLs, which appear nowhere in core
config or in any document format, so it is harmless -- but dropping ucpext too
would make such a URL fail cleanly instead of throwing.

RISK / TEST

Lower risk than the cui removal: the consumers that exist already handle the
"no extension manager" case explicitly, and the two unhandled sites are both
proven unreachable. A regression would appear as a DeploymentException in the
[Wasm stderr] log at shutdown or during a conversion.

Test: full pipeline (`./pipeline/build_and_deploy.sh`), with particular
attention to Phase 7's page-refresh and module-stress tests -- those exercise
repeated lo_destroy/re-init, which is the only place a shutdown-path throw could
surface. `node tests/test_page_refresh.js` is the targeted one.

diff --git a/desktop/Library_deployment.mk b/desktop/Library_deployment.mk
--- a/desktop/Library_deployment.mk
+++ b/desktop/Library_deployment.mk
@@ -37,7 +37,30 @@
     i18nlangtag \
 ))
 
+# WASM: do NOT register the component file. See the long note in
+# cui/Library_cui.mk -- solenv/gbuild/static.mk:66-67 force-links every library
+# that has one into the static `components` library, and native-code.py names
+# its constructors in a static map, so nothing can be dead-stripped.
+#
+# --disable-extensions does NOT do this. It only sets HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS=0,
+# which stubs a handful of #if blocks INSIDE these still-compiled-and-linked
+# sources; there is no DISABLE_EXTENSIONS make variable anywhere in the tree and
+# Library_deployment is in Module_desktop.mk unconditionally.
+#
+# All ten com_sun_star_comp_deployment_* constructors live here. A converter
+# with a read-only install and zero installed extensions never needs any of
+# them: configmgr's bundledext/sharedext/userext layers are plain file reads of
+# configmgr.ini files that do not exist, filter/source/config/cache/ never
+# consults the deployment registry, and every remaining consumer either catches
+# DeploymentException (linguistic/source/lngsvcmgr.cxx:424,
+# svx/source/smarttags/SmartTagMgr.cxx:446) or is compiled out.
+#
+# Library_deploymentmisc is deliberately NOT touched: sofficeapp hard-links it
+# for DpResId (desktop/source/deployment/misc/dp_misc.cxx:560), which every
+# bootstrap error string in desktop/source/app/app.cxx uses.
+ifneq ($(OS),EMSCRIPTEN)
 $(eval $(call gb_Library_set_componentfile,deployment,desktop/source/deployment/deployment,services))
+endif
 
 $(eval $(call gb_Library_add_exception_objects,deployment,\
     desktop/source/deployment/dp_log \
diff --git a/desktop/Library_deploymentgui.mk b/desktop/Library_deploymentgui.mk
--- a/desktop/Library_deploymentgui.mk
+++ b/desktop/Library_deploymentgui.mk
@@ -54,7 +54,16 @@
 endif
 
 
+# WASM: do NOT register the component file -- same mechanism as
+# desktop/Library_deployment.mk. The three services here (LicenseDialog,
+# PackageManagerDialog, UpdateRequiredDialog) all require a real VCL window and
+# a user, which a headless converter has neither of. Their only in-tree callers
+# are desktop/source/app/check_ext_deps.cxx:140/:223, reached only when an
+# INSTALLED extension has unsatisfied dependencies, and
+# cui/source/factory/dlgfact.cxx:1553, which is #if HAVE_FEATURE_EXTENSIONS-dead.
+ifneq ($(OS),EMSCRIPTEN)
 $(eval $(call gb_Library_set_componentfile,deploymentgui,desktop/source/deployment/gui/deploymentgui,services))
+endif
 
 $(eval $(call gb_Library_add_exception_objects,deploymentgui,\
     desktop/source/deployment/gui/dp_gui_dependencydialog \
diff --git a/comphelper/source/misc/backupfilehelper.cxx b/comphelper/source/misc/backupfilehelper.cxx
--- a/comphelper/source/misc/backupfilehelper.cxx
+++ b/comphelper/source/misc/backupfilehelper.cxx
@@ -385,10 +385,20 @@
             // create content from current extension configuration
             uno::Sequence< uno::Sequence< uno::Reference< deployment::XPackage > > > xAllPackages;
             const uno::Reference< uno::XComponentContext >& xContext = ::comphelper::getProcessComponentContext();
-            uno::Reference< deployment::XExtensionManager > m_xExtensionManager = deployment::ExtensionManager::get(xContext);
 
             try
             {
+                // Acquiring the service must be inside the try: if the extension
+                // manager is not registered at all (a build without the
+                // deployment component -- e.g. WASM, see
+                // desktop/Library_deployment.mk) then ExtensionManager::get()
+                // throws DeploymentException, and this function is called from
+                // Desktop::doShutdown() via tryPushExtensionInfo() with nothing
+                // above it to catch. "No extension manager" means "no extension
+                // info to back up", which is exactly the existing
+                // DeploymentException handler below.
+                uno::Reference< deployment::XExtensionManager > m_xExtensionManager = deployment::ExtensionManager::get(xContext);
+
                 xAllPackages = m_xExtensionManager->getAllExtensions(uno::Reference< task::XAbortChannel >(),
                     uno::Reference< ucb::XCommandEnvironment >());
             }
